  class A { void show() { System.out.println("A"); } }
  class B extends A { void show() { System.out.println("B"); } }
  A obj = new B();
  obj.show();', 'The overridden method is chosen at runtime from the actual object type (B), not from the reference type (A). This is runtime polymorphism.', TRUE);
  class P { static void f() { System.out.println("P"); } }
  class C extends P { static void f() { System.out.println("C"); } }
  P p = new C();
  p.f();', 'Static methods are hidden, not overridden. The call is bound at compile time using the reference type P.', TRUE);
